{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the number of possible sequences of length n, such that each element is a positive integer\n    and is greater than or equal to twice the previous element but less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n\n    # dp_current[j] stores the number of sequences of current_length ending with j.\n    # prefix_sum_current[j] stores the sum of dp_current[k] for 1 <= k <= j.\n    # We only need the previous row's dp and prefix_sum to calculate the current row,\n    # so we use two arrays to optimize space.\n\n    # Initialize for length = 1: each number from 1 to m can be the first element.\n    prev_dp = [0] * (m + 1)\n    prev_prefix_sum = [0] * (m + 1)\n    \n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        prev_dp[j] = 1\n        prev_prefix_sum[j] = prev_prefix_sum[j - 1] + prev_dp[j]\n\n    # Iterate for lengths from 2 to n\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        current_dp = [0] * (m + 1)\n        current_prefix_sum = [0] * (m + 1)\n        \n        for j in range(1, m + 1):\n            # The previous element (a_k-1) must be <= floor(j / 2).\n            max_prev_val_allowed = j // 2 \n            \n            if max_prev_val_allowed >= 1:\n                # The count of sequences ending with j is the sum of sequences of (current_length-1)\n                # whose last element is <= max_prev_val_allowed. This sum is efficiently retrieved\n                # from the previous prefix sum array.\n                current_dp[j] = prev_prefix_sum[max_prev_val_allowed]\n            # If max_prev_val_allowed < 1 (i.e., j=1), current_dp[j] remains 0 as no previous element is possible.\n        \n        # Calculate prefix sum for the current_length\n        for j in range(1, m + 1):\n            current_prefix_sum[j] = current_prefix_sum[j - 1] + current_dp[j]\n            \n        # Update previous arrays for the next iteration\n        prev_dp = current_dp\n        prev_prefix_sum = current_prefix_sum\n\n    # The total number of sequences of length n is the sum of dp[n][j] for all j from 1 to m,\n    # which is stored in prev_prefix_sum[m] after the loop completes for n.\n    return prev_prefix_sum[m]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef max_sum(arr: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array, where a sequence is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    This implementation uses dynamic programming to calculate LIS and LDS sums for each element, then combines them.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    # Calculate LIS sums (maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at index i)\n    lis_sum = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n):\n        lis_sum[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:  # Strict increasing comparison\n                lis_sum[i] = max(lis_sum[i], lis_sum[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Calculate LDS sums (maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at index i)\n    lds_sum = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        lds_sum[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:  # Strict decreasing comparison\n                lds_sum[i] = max(lds_sum[i], lds_sum[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Combine LIS and LDS sums to find the maximum bitonic sum.\n    # For a bitonic subsequence with peak arr[i], the sum is LIS_sum[i] + LDS_sum[i] - arr[i]\n    # (arr[i] is counted once as the peak).\n    max_bitonic_sum = float('-inf') # Initialize with negative infinity to handle potentially negative sums\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sum[i] + lds_sum[i] - arr[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
